course: dictionary
lesson: 6447
title: Words from family and home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one family, one place or one kind of talk. Nanna is one of them. «In Brisbane, Nanna buys Ava-Rose an ice cream every arvo» tells you that Nanna is a person who buys treats. Arvo is another new word: it means afternoon, so Nanna buys the ice cream in the afternoon.
explain: Who is Nanna? Look for clues. Ava-Rose is a child, and Nanna buys her ice cream, so Nanna is probably a grandmother. In the next lines, Mum says, «She'll rot her teeth!» and Nanna answers, «She's a growing girl!» That tells you Nanna is a close family member who is happy to spoil Ava-Rose a little.
explain: Be careful with jokes. «You're such a nanna» does not mean you have a grandmother. It is a joke that says you act old or fussy for your age. Check by swapping in your meaning: if someone fusses like a grandmother, does the sentence still make sense? Yes, so the joke means you are being fussy.
fact: Nanna means grandmother, and it is what a child often calls their gran.
fact: Nanna is also spelled nana or nan, and people in Australia and New Zealand use it a lot in family talk.
fact: In a joke, «You're such a nanna» means you act old-fashioned or fussy.
fact: In Australia, a nanna nap is a short sleep during the day.
fact: When Nanna is a name, it starts with a capital letter, as in «We're going to Nanna's for lunch».
exercise: «In Brisbane, Nanna buys Ava-Rose an ice cream every arvo.» Who is Nanna most likely to be? | A pet dog | *A grandmother | A teacher at school | A park in Brisbane
exercise: What does arvo mean in «buys Ava-Rose an ice cream every arvo»? | Morning | Night | *Afternoon | Weekend
exercise: Someone says, «You're such a nanna» after you fuss over your bag. What does it mean? | You are a kind person | *You act old or fussy for your age | You have a grandmother who lives with you | You are very tired and need a nap
test: In Australia, what is a nanna nap? | A long trip to the beach | A big family lunch | *A short sleep during the day | A game played at night
test: Mum says, «She'll rot her teeth!» Nanna says, «She's a growing girl!» What does Nanna think about the ice cream? | *She thinks Ava-Rose can have it | She is cross and wants it thrown away | She thinks ice cream is bad for everyone | She is asleep and has not heard
exam: Which is another spelling of nanna used in Australia and New Zealand? | Grandad | *Nana | Nanny's house | Granpa
